senses.gloss:
(I)--a mind-born son of ब्रह्मा born with नारद at the beginning of creation;
1: भा. I. 6. ३१; III. १२. २२; IX. 1. १०; Br. II. ३२. ९६; III. 1. २१, ४३-4; M. 3. 6; 4. २६; १९५. 9.
married कला a daughter of Kardama;
2: भा. III. २४. २२; IV. 1. १३.
father of कश्यप;
3: Ib. III. १४. 7; २०. १०.
came with ब्रह्मा to see Kapila born to Kardama;
4: Ib. III. २४. 9.
was present in दक्ष's यज्ञ;
5: Ib. IV. 7. ४३; २९. ४३.
directed the अश्वमेध of Indra;
6: Ib. VI. १३. २१.
came to see the Trivikrama अवतार् of the Lord;
7: Ib. VIII. २१. 1.
did not comprehend Hari's माय।
8: Ib. IX. 4. ५८.
The chief sage of Vena's reign responsible for punishing him. A sage in दारुवन;
9: Br. II. २१. ११५; २७. १०४; ३६. १३३; III. १०. ५२; M. १४५. ९०; १५४. ३५२; १७१. २७.
one of the seven sages of स्वायम्भुव epoch: instructed by ब्रह्मा on the eighteen पुराणस्; praised शिव, out to destroy Tripuram;
१०: Ib. 9. 4; ५३. १२; १०२. १९; १२७. २४; १३३. ६७.
had a daughter सुरूपा, whom Angiras got married.
११: Ib. १९६. 1; २४५. ८६; २५०. 4.
[page२-637+ ३१]

(V)--a sage of the स्वायम्भुव epoch;
1: वा. 3. 2; ३१. १६; ६२. ११३; ६५. ४४.
son-in- law of दक्ष;
2: Ib. ३०. ४८.
married सम्भूती;
3: Br. II. 9. ५५; वा. २८. 8; Vi. I. १०. 6; ११. ४३.
advised Dhruva to pray to विष्णु.
4: Ib. I. १२. 6.

(I)--fortynine in number, born of Diti and कश्यप; seven in each of the seven वातस्कन्धस्; brothers of Indra and participators in sacrifices;
1: भा. VI. १८. १९, २३-77: VIII. १३. 4: Br. III. 5. ७९, ९०, ९९, १०४: M. 6. ४७; १६३. २२-3.
when Diti conceived a son to be the slayer of Indra, the latter began to serve her throughout her pregnancy. Once finding that she did not keep to her vows he entered her womb and cut the foetus into ४९ pieces, when they cried. He said to them मा रुद and hence मारुत: being divine, were born as ४९ sons: at the request of their mother Indra made them a देवगण, called मरुत्गण.
2: M. Ch. 7.
Gods of the Vaivasvata epoch, Indra being their over- lord: requested Soma to give up तारा to बृहस्पति.
3: Ib. 8. 4: 9. २९: २३. ३५: ३६. 1.
Fought with निवातकवचस् in the देवासुर war: mounted guards in Marutta's यज्ञस्: nourished भरद्वाज abandoned by ममता and gave him to Bharata as his son;
4: भा. VI. १०. १७: IX. 2. २८; २०. ३५-9: M. ४९. १५, २५-30: ५८. ३३.
helped Indra in the heavy downpour on Nandavraja: went with the gods to द्वारका to request कृष्ण to go back to वैकुण्ठ;
5: भा. X. २५. 7: XI. 6. 2.
Fathers of शोभवत्य group of Apsarasas; presiding deity of कालोपनत मूर्छन; line in Bhuvar- loka and लोकालोक: perform श्राद्ध;
6: Br. III. 7. २०: ६१. ४६: IV. 2. २७, १९७: III. १०. ११०.
are worshipped for lasting strength (ओजस्)।
7: भा. II. 3. 8.
Their service in the battle of Tripuram: Shaken by हिरण्यकशिपु; glad at Hari's attack on the Asuras;
8: M. ५८. ३३: १३२. 3; १३७. १८; १७२. १४-44; १७४. ३२.
attain- ed सिद्धि at सिद्देश्वरम्;
9: Ib. १९१. ११७; २४६. ६०.
companions of those who are devoted to their brothers;
१०: भा. VI. 5. ३१.
brought up भरद्वाज, son of बृहस्पति.
११: वा. ९९. १३९-51.

(I)--the seven pieces of Diti's गर्भ be- came seven गणस् in the वायु मार्ग; each originated seven
1: वा. ३०. ९९: ६४. 2: Vi. I. 9. ६४ and ७०: २१. ४०.
गणस् in turn and thus ४९ Marut गणस् are distinguished; they partake in यज्ञस् especially गरुड शयन यज्ञ;
2: वा. ६७. ११०, १२३-29.
residents of Bhuvarloka;
3: Ib. १०१. २९.
part of विष्णु;
4: Vi. V. 1. १७.
see शक्र.

--(शण्ड) an Asura; one of the four sons of शुक्र and a tutor of प्रह्लाद;
1: भा. VII. 5. 1-2, ४८-50; Br. III. 1. ७८; ७२. ७२, ८७; ७३. ६३-4; M. ४७. ४१; वा. ६५. ७७.
seen by the Gods at the sacrifice;
2: M. ४७. ५४.
one of the two disciples the other being शण्ड of शुक्र sent to help the Asuras; but he joined the camp of the Devas, the latter offering him a place in sacrifices.
3: Ib. ४७. २२४-31; वा. ९७. ७२ and ८६; ९८. ६३; १०८. ६०.

(III)--(मारीचकश्यप): a son of अन्तर्धान and grandson of पृथु;
1: M. 4. ४५.
his wife Vasu abandoned him for Soma;
2: Ib. २३. २५.
his sons are said to reside in the Somapatha worlds of the पितृस्.
3: Ib. १४. 1.

(I)--a Siddha not lost in deluge;
1: भा. VI. १५. १२; M. 2. १३; १८६-3.
son of मृकण्ड;
2: भा. IV. 1. ४५.
his firm and non-parallelled तपस् and vow of [page२-694+ ३९] celibacy; saw the पुरुष sleeping on a leaf of the वटवृक्स; his आश्रम near the हिमालयस् on a शिल-citra; Indra sent the God of Love, Apsaras and others to disturb him, but in vain; the महात्मा, seeing Hari in Nara-नारायण form praised him; pleased with him as one who would be ever meditating on his feet Hari showed him what a प्रलय was; पार्वती and शिव. saw him, and were praised; when शिव offered to grant him anything he wanted, he expressed his wish to be ever devoted to him and Hari; pleased with him शिव went away with पार्वती; this worthy son of the भृगु race having earned Yogic vision and absolutely devoted to Hari even now goes about the world;
3: Ib. XII. Chh. 8, 9 and १०.
an authority on राम's story.
4: Ib. VII. 1. ४४.

(II)--a contemporary of दत्तात्रेय; Purohita, the fourth incarnation of दात्तात्रेय, born to help him;
1: Br. II. ३३. ११; III. ७३. ८९; M. ४७. २४२; ५३. २६; वा. ९८. ८९; १०९. २४; ११२. ३४.
narrated the मार्कण्डेय पुराण;
2: M. ४७. २४२; ५३. २६.
acted as ब्रह्मा in परशुराम's sacrifice.
3: Br. III. ४७. ४६; IV. ३९. ५५.

(IV)--a son of मनस्विनी and मृकण्डु;
1: वा. २८. 5; Vi. I. १०. 4.
wife धूम्रपत्नी and son वेदशिरस्;
2: Br. II. ११. 7.
present at राम's अभिषेक.
3: Vi. IV. 4. ९९.

(I)--the Sun God; ब्रह्मा placed the तेजस् of the अण्डम् in the गर्भ of अदिती and when everything became stunted, the God removed it from the गर्भ mak- [page२-697+ ३३] ing it into two pieces; finding the weakness of the गर्भ ब्रह्मा caused it to be placed in the lap of the Sun God; hence the name;
1: Br. III. 7. २७५-288; M. 2. ३५.
another ety.:--when कश्यप found the universe divided into two, he was in distress and said you be मर्ताण्ड or विवस्वान्, son of कश्यप and दाक्षायनी; had seven sons; सावर्णि and शनैश्चर are the last;
2: वा. ८४. २५.
R. यमुना, the daughter of;
3: Br. III. १३. ७२.
नासत्य and Dasra, sons of;
4: Ib. III. ५९. २५; IV. ३८. २३.
golden image of, for gift;
5: M. 9. 3; २८०. 6.
मण्डलम् of.
6: Br. I. 1. ११५.
